  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>if</keyword>
<keyword_alias>block:if</keyword_alias>
  <short_description>Selects an action output from a boolean expression over the inputs.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Block type: if</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>input ports</param_name>
      <param_description>The signals u1..un referenced by the expressions.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output ports</param_name>
      <param_description>One output for the if clause, one per elseif, plus an optional else output.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Selects an action output from a boolean expression over the inputs.</p>
    <p>The if clause and each elseif clause are evaluated in order over the inputs
    <code>u1..un</code>; the first true clause drives its output to <code>1.0</code> and every
    other output to <code>0.0</code>. With <code>ShowElse</code> set to <code>on</code>, an
    all-false result drives the last (else) output. The expression grammar is restricted:
    comparisons (<code>&lt; &lt;= &gt; &gt;= == ~=</code>), logic (<code>&amp; | ~</code>),
    parentheses, unary minus, numeric literals and <code>u&lt;k&gt;</code> inputs. These outputs
    are meant to gate action subsystems.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Parameters</b>
    </p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Parameter</th>
          <th>Default value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>IfExpression</code>
          </td>
          <td>u1 &gt; 0</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>ElseIfExpressions</code>
          </td>
          <td>(comma-separated, empty by default)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>ShowElse</code>
          </td>
          <td>on</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <b>Block Characteristics</b>
    </p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Block type</td>
          <td>if</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Family</td>
          <td>Logic blocks</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Phases</td>
          <td>ALGEBRAIC</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Extended Capabilities</b></p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
  </description>
